  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The house descends from the clouds toward Fang Yuan while he cultivates. He reads its mixed rank seven Immortal Gu aura on woodwork thick with flowers.",
      "chapters": [
        1512
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As it lands, petals rain down, turn desert sand to mud, and raise a sea of flowers. Fang An Lei, Fang Yun, and Fang Leng come out to thank him and invite him inside for talks; he treats the house as strong outside and weak inside, the common Immortal Gu House pattern, and walks in.",
      "chapters": [
        1513
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_an_lei",
        "char_fang_yun",
        "char_fang_leng",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Under Fang An Lei’s control the house flies up to evade a grasping immemorial soul beast, then slams a winged black python and cracks across its exterior before a shining repair restores cracks and flowers in a few breaths. Fang Yuan notes that most Immortal Gu Houses lack such rapid self-repair. Eagle Concubine later claws three deep marks into the roof, forcing Fang An Lei to ask Fang Yuan for help.",
      "chapters": [
        1514
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "combat-self-repair",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_eagle_concubine"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang An Lei uses mirror flower to absorb Eagle Concubine’s claw marks into mirrored petals and shoot them into Divine Bean Palace, then fleeting bloom to slow a flying spider immemorial soul beast. Fang Yuan judges both wood path killer moves, with rule path and time path flavors, and Fang An Lei ranks Fallen Flower Hall among the top of rank seven Immortal Gu Houses while still calling the enemy force too much to handle.",
      "chapters": [
        1517
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "killer-move-fielding",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Empty valley orchid then shrinks the house and stretches space so Divine Bean Palace must travel a huge distance to close; Fallen Flower Hall is still inferior to the rank eight palace when the two collide.",
      "chapters": [
        1518
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "palace-collision",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan lists mirror flower, fleeting bloom, and empty valley orchid among the house’s killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        1519
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "killer-move-list",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Di Chang later plans to repair Fallen Flower Hall and combine it with Chicken Dog Coop and Inquiry Dock into the battlefield killer move peach blossom maze to trap Divine Bean Palace.",
      "chapters": [
        1520
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "repair-and-combination",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_di_chang",
        "house_chicken_dog_coop",
        "house_inquiry_dock",
        "house_divine_bean_palace"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Fallen Flower Hall is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment of Fang clan, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
